1. Enable Nesting (Proxmox Web UI)

Required for GPU + TUN access.

CT → Options → Features → Enable "Nesting"

2. LXC Container: Base System Setup

Run inside the container.

apt update
apt upgrade -y

apt install -y \
  pve-headers-$(uname -r) \
  build-essential make gcc g++ cmake git \
  pkg-config curl unzip sudo \
  ffmpeg nvtop htop \
  xserver-xorg-dev xserver-xorg-core \
  libglvnd-dev

update-initramfs -u

3. Clean Previous NVIDIA / CUDA (Recommended)

Run inside the container.

sudo apt purge -y 'nvidia-*' 'cuda-*' 'libnvidia-*'
sudo apt autoremove --purge -y

4. Install CUDA + NVIDIA Driver (Debian 12 Example — Update Version If Needed)

Check latest version:
https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit

Run inside the container:

wget https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/13.0.2/local_installers/cuda-repo-debian12-13-0-local_13.0.2-580.95.05-1_amd64.deb

sudo dpkg -i cuda-repo-debian12-13-0-local_13.0.2-580.95.05-1_amd64.deb
sudo cp /var/cuda-repo-debian12-13-0-local/cuda-*-keyring.gpg /usr/share/keyrings/

sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y nvidia-open cuda-toolkit-13-0

Add CUDA to PATH
echo 'export PATH=/usr/local/cuda/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.bashrc
echo 'export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/cuda/lib64:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

5. Verify GPU Device Nodes (Host)

Run on Proxmox host:

ls -al /dev/nvidia*


You should see:

/dev/nvidia0
/dev/nvidiactl
/dev/nvidia-uvm
/dev/nvidia-uvm-tools
/dev/nvidia-caps/*


Important device majors:

195 → nvidia
505 → uvm
508 → caps

6. Enable GPU + Tailscale Access in LXC Config (Host)

Edit container config:

/etc/pve/lxc/<CTID>.conf


Add:

# NVIDIA
lxc.cgroup2.devices.allow: c 195:* rwm
lxc.cgroup2.devices.allow: c 505:* rwm
lxc.cgroup2.devices.allow: c 508:* rwm

lxc.mount.entry: /dev/nvidia0 dev/nvidia0 none bind,optional,create=file
lxc.mount.entry: /dev/nvidiactl dev/nvidiactl none bind,optional,create=file
lxc.mount.entry: /dev/nvidia-modeset dev/nvidia-modeset none bind,optional,create=file

# Tailscale / tun
lxc.cgroup2.devices.allow: c 10:200 rwm
lxc.mount.entry: /dev/net/tun dev/net/tun none bind,create=file


Restart container after.

7. Optional: Push NVIDIA Run Installer to Container (Host)

If using .run installer:

pct push <CTID> Nvidia.run /Nvidia.run

8. Optional: 32-bit Support + Additional Packages
dpkg --add-architecture i386
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y

sudo apt install -y \
  build-essential gcc g++ make cmake git \
  pkg-config curl unzip sudo ffmpeg \
  xserver-xorg-dev xserver-xorg-core \
  libglvnd-dev

9. Full Driver Reinstall (If Things Break)

Use this if CUDA/NVIDIA gets messy.

sudo apt remove --purge -y 'nvidia*' 'cuda*'
sudo apt autoremove --purge -y

sudo rm -rf /usr/local/cuda*
sudo rm -f /etc/apt/sources.list.d/cuda*
sudo rm -rf /var/cuda-repo-*

sudo apt update


Then repeat Section 4.


if [ -d /opt/cuda ]; then
    export CUDA_HOME=/opt/cuda
    export PATH="$CUDA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$CUDA_HOME/lib64:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH"
fi
